  "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
  "body": "I'm trying to run on bitnet a fine-tuned model of `Llama3-8B-1.58-100B-tokens`. The model was already quantized dynamically, however it seems mandatory to convert the model to the gguf model format. Let me know if you think I'm doing something wrong. \n\nLooking at the table [here](https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet?tab=readme-ov-file#supported-models), it seems that for running the `Llama3-8B-1.58-100B-tokens` model on arm is necessary to quantize using `tl2`, however, when I try to run the `setup_env.py` I get this: \n\n```\nusage: setup_env.py [-h] [--hf-repo {1bitLLM/bitnet_b1_58-large,1bitLLM/bitnet_b1_58-3B,HF1BitLLM/Llama3-8B-1.58-100B-tokens}]\n                    [--model-dir MODEL_DIR] [--log-dir LOG_DIR] [--quant-type {i2_s,tl1}] [--quant-embd] [--use-pretuned]\nsetup_env.py: error: argument --quant-type/-q: invalid choice: 'tl2' (choose from 'i2_s', 'tl1')\n```\n\nso is it possible to use tl2 for quantization? ",
  "closed_at": "2024-12-05T08:17:24Z",
